caption: Classes and Functions — Classes and Functions
technology-rule: classes-and-functions

Class measures visibility and body-plan impact. Category measures the role of the modification in the character build. These are separate decisions.

| Class | Definition | Quick Test | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| I - Internal / Covert | Hidden, internal, or natural-looking. | Can you pass casual inspection? | Datajack, artificial heart, natural cyber-eye, subdermal armor |
| II - Obvious / Anatomical | Visible, but preserves normal species anatomy. | Are you still shaped like your species? | Chrome arm, cyberlegs, visible eye, power spine |
| III - Transformative / Chassis | Changes body plan or makes the body a platform. | Has your body become a chassis? | Tracks, spider body, turret, total conversion |

| Category | What It Does | Typical Point Treatment | Example |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Restorative | Restores lost or damaged function. | Mitigator or net trait difference. | Replacement hand or artificial heart |
| Practical | Adds tools, communication, or convenience. | Accessory, perk, small advantage, or equipment. | Datajack or biomonitor |
| Performance | Improves combat, survival, senses, movement, or cognition. | Full point cost after real limitations. | Subdermal armor or reflex governor |
| Transformative | Changes body assumptions, scale, or identity. | Template, lens, Alternate Form, or rebuild. | Spider chassis or total cyborg body |

| Edge Case | Usual Class | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Natural-looking cyberarm | I apparent / II functional | It may pass visually but is still a replaceable limb system. |
| Cyber-tail on a tailed species | II | It preserves species anatomy. |
| Heavy scorpion tail added to a human | III | It changes body plan and combat reach. |
| Mechanical wings on a winged species | II | Replacement of expected anatomy. |
| Reactionless flight pack built into a human torso | III | The body becomes a flight platform. |
| Wrist gun | II | Fits within an anatomical limb. |
| Shoulder turret | III | Mounted like a vehicle weapon. |

| Cybernetic | Base Function | Added Function | Controlling Category |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Normal bionic hand | Restores a hand | None | Restorative |
| Strong bionic hand | Restores a hand | Arm ST and local DR | Restorative + Performance |
| Datajack | Direct interface | None | Practical |
| Datajack with cyberdeck | Direct interface | Hacking and defense suite | Practical + Performance |
| Artificial lung | Restores breathing | Filter Lungs and reserve air | Restorative + Performance |
| Rescue chassis | Saves a life | New machine body | Transformative |

APPARENT VS. FUNCTIONAL CLASS

A human-looking total body may pass as Class I while remaining functional Class III for repair, damage, and templates.
